== BLOCKER-7E-2 (alloc-first-then-free) ==
Code review assertion: realloc_buf/ensure_weight_slot/AttentionWorkspace::ensure/pinned-slab growth
all hipMalloc/hipHostMalloc into a fresh pointer BEFORE freeing the old buffer; on allocation failure the
exception is raised with the previous buffer still valid and owned, so no destructor/next-growth double
free exists. drain() before free remains. LayerGuard is armed only during unwinding, so an ensure() failure
at layer entry (before any async work) needs no drain: nothing is in flight. No reproduceable failure-path
test (hipMalloc failure cannot be injected without kernel changes) - the pattern is enforced by review and
covered by the existing exception-after-enqueue test for the enqueue-side failure.

